  "notes": [
    "Three complete Ghidra-analyzed standard cdecl bodies: formation creation returns a DWORD id, recruitment and refresh have void contracts.",
    "Formation records have stride144, actor records388. Native formation colours are0..7 and impose the same eight-byte local-palette precondition.",
    "Refresh clears groups1..49, scans actors1..1999, retains the native16-member list limit and BYTE/WORD/DWORD wrap without clamping the actor count.",
    "Recruitment caches the source building's owner address, reloads current-player ingress coordinates and rally target each iteration, then always refreshes even for nonpositive counts.",
    "The original47D350 is a nullary return-zero placeholder; its caller pushes158 but the callee ignores it. Preserve the actual callee rather than inventing a notification.",
    "Removed nonmilitary groups deduplicate signed event ids, cancel removal for surviving groups, and clear the native event-record BYTE+50 only after the final scan."
  ]
